187
00:11:58,520 --> 00:11:59,400
6,800.

188
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:01,040
6,600.

189
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:02,870
Damn it.

190
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:06,532
We're dropping like a sack of
rocks, but I don't know why.

191
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:09,640
As to why we're losing
altitude, I have the answer.

192
00:12:09,820 --> 00:12:14,580
But even so, I'm at a complete
loss regarding what to do about it.

193
00:12:15,140 --> 00:12:17,640
I hate to say it, but I'm stumped here.

194
00:12:18,060 --> 00:12:20,337
What the heck are you
talking about, Bucurati?

195
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:22,067
What did I say about moving?

196
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:23,430
No.

197
00:12:23,660 --> 00:12:24,580
Please, no.

198
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:27,040
Wait, what? There's no way.

199
00:12:27,380 --> 00:12:29,177
How the hell did it even...

200
00:12:29,260 --> 00:12:32,220
Giorno said the beast
latches onto moving objects.

201
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:34,557
Once they're captured, it devours them.

202
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:36,097
Right now, the plane's engines...

203
00:12:36,180 --> 00:12:38,380
